WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.976 --> 00:00:06.461
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.900
 I think it's absolutely
insane that Kamala is actually

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:14.440
going to be in one of
the biggest Marvel games

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.710
that we've done.

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:18.180
BILL ROSEMANN: She's
a very recent addition

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:18.990
to the Marvel universe.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.580
She was only invented--

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.140
gosh, about six years ago.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:25.020
But even though she's very
new, she's very classic.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:29.250
SANA AMANAT: She is a young
hero from Jersey City,

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.220
and she has something called
polymorph powers, which means

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:35.020
she can contort her
body in different ways,

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:37.110
and she can get really
big, and really small.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:40.140
 We spent countless
hours on the story,

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.290
on the choice of character,
how we would portray her.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.240
 I loved working
with Shaun Escayg

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:48.420
and the rest of the creative
team at Crystal Dynamics.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.730
To sit down with Shaun and
talk about the characters,

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:51.870
and how he saw them.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:54.960
 To stay true to her, we spent
a lot of time in the comics,

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:58.230
and then also tapping
into our version of her.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:01.380
 The biggest difference between
our game and the Kamala people

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:06.660
have met in the comics, she
gains her powers on A day.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.750
SANA AMANAT: She is essentially
just a little fan girl, right?

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:10.860
She's a nerd.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:12.330
She loves the Marvel universe.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.580
She lives in the
Marvel universe.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.800
 Her fan fiction
comic is selected

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.223
for the Avengers celebrations.

00:01:18.223 --> 00:01:19.590
HANNAH MCLEOD: The
Avengers are unveiling

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:24.360
this experimental technology,
and something pretty crazy

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.530
happens with it.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.360
SHAUN ESCAYG: She's
exposed to Terrigen gas,

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:30.810
and is now labeled what
is called an Inhuman.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:32.190
HANNAH MCLEOD: She's
got Super Powers

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:34.620
that she doesn't know
what to do is in a world

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.750
that hates Super Heroes.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.970
BILL ROSEMANN: She
suspects that the Avengers

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:40.710
were set up in A Day.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:44.190
The role that Kamala
plays is a unifier.

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:47.280
She's really someone
who is going to bring

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.370
the Avengers back together.

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:55.030
 Casting Kamala was
a difficult process.

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:58.570
We spent a lot of time
looking for Sandra,

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:02.045
and she did an impeccable
job bringing her life.

00:02:02.045 --> 00:02:03.550
 Oh, my god.

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:06.010
When I found out I was going to
play the role of Kamala Khan,

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:08.600
I was like, are you kidding?

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.030
I'm an Avenger?

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:13.070
 She's a lot like the
character in many ways.

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:15.730
So there's instant
believability.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:19.390
SANDRA SAAD: She is a first
generation American, like me.

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:21.370
She's a young woman
of color who has

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:23.680
trouble fitting in, like I do.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:26.920
And I feel like she has all
these personal struggles

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.140
that everyone can relate to.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.600
 In the cast of
seasoned actors,

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:36.220
she is the new one in some
sense that that forced structure

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:38.170
between the seasoned
actors and the new actor

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.930
is sort of like
the actual Kamala

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:46.090
Khan relationship to her
world, and to her environment.

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:48.520
 We wanted to really
focus on her gameplay,

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.140
and her style of
moves reflecting

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:51.730
her development as a character.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:55.450
So you might notice that there's
at least one or two attacks

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:57.340
that she's sort of,
like, made her own

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:58.510
from the other
Avengers, and sort

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.280
of integrated into our moveset.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.080
One of the most iconic
things about Kamala

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.050
is her ability to embiggen,
and we actually realized this

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:06.250
in a bunch of different ways.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:07.810
She's able to, like,
lengthen her attacks,

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:09.790
she's able to avoid
attacks while she sort

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:11.320
of mini-embiggens.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:13.270
And then we also have
the ultra-embiggen state

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:14.940
where she gets giant sized.

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:17.410
And at this point, she's
able to send enemies flying.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:19.300
We actually built an
entirely new reaction

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.790
set for the enemies to,
like, really deliver on

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:23.860
the feel of being,
you know, three times,

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:25.690
four times the
size of the enemies

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:27.040
you're sort of kicking around.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.373
SANDRA SAAD: Putting
together a movement

00:03:28.373 --> 00:03:31.960
style for Kamala is just all
in the imagination, I feel.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:33.460
Because at the end
of the day, it's

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:37.300
you who's standing there
in this mocap space,

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:40.360
imagining that your
arm, Sandra's arm,

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:44.200
is stretching out to the end
of the room to grab somebody.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:47.550
It's just fun.

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:50.400
I hope the fans notice
those little details,

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.720
and I hope the fans see how
hard every single person worked.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:57.720
And I hope the fans love
the story as much as I do.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:00.600
 When it comes to a new
perspective on the Avengers,

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.720
seeing them from a
fan girl, of someone

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.870
who has always wanted to meet
them, has wanted to be one--

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:09.820
we feel like players can
really connect with that.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:11.280
SANA AMANAT: Marvel
has considered her

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.320
an important enough
character to be

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.090
on the League of the Avengers.

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:16.709
SHAUN ESCAYG: She's
got Super Hero powers

00:04:16.709 --> 00:04:18.630
unlike any other Avenger.

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:20.870
She's not laying
down for no one,

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:23.940
and I think those qualities,
they cross boundaries.

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:24.900
People can relate to it.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:26.040
She's rebellious.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.570
They want to be her.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.160
I want to be her.

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:32.700
 The fact that she is the entry
point character in this game

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:36.620
makes so much sense because
she really is the everyman.

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:39.750
Like, people from all
backgrounds and experiences

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.640
can relate to her,
and have related

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.200
to her since her inception.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.090
So it makes perfect
sense for her

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.910
to be bringing you
into the "Marvel

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:50.870
Avengers" game experience.

